.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH loom-session 1  "loom-session " 
.SH NAME
loom\-session \- Session lifecycle commands (RPC)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBloom\-session\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Session lifecycle commands (RPC)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
loom\-session\-create(1)
`loom session create` arguments. Flag names mirror the `session.create` RPC request schema
.TP
loom\-session\-inspect(1)
`loom session inspect <id>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-list(1)
`loom session list` arguments. Empty body — flags are global
.TP
loom\-session\-close(1)
`loom session close <id>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-abort(1)
`loom session abort <id>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-replay(1)
`loom session replay <id>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-diff(1)
`loom session diff <a> <b>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-export(1)
`loom session export <id> \-\-format ...` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-validate(1)
`loom session validate <id>` arguments
.TP
loom\-session\-reap(1)
`session reap [\-\-apply]` — quarantine corrupt\-WAL orphan sessions that are stuck in the active set and consuming concurrency slots. Previews by default (dry\-run); pass `\-\-apply` to actually move them aside
.TP
loom\-session\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
